<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sunnmøre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sunnmøre is the southernmost traditional district of the county of Møre og <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romsdal">Romsdal</a> on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, with Ålesund as its main town. Its fjords include the Geirangerfjord, a World Heritage Site. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>, with North Møre, it formed the earldom of Møre held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rognvald-eysteinsson">Rognvald Eysteinsson</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sunnmore.jpg" alt="Sunnmøre" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pilum at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunnmore-region.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
